# Input data. Third-party scientific data — an atomic mass evaluation, charge distribution and
# shell correction systematics, a resonance parameter library, and experimental fragment mass
# yields. None of it originates with this package and the licence on this code does not extend
# to it, so it is held locally and documented rather than redistributed. data/README.md records
# what each file is and where to obtain it, and is tracked.
#
# The atomic mass evaluation ships with FissionFragmentsDomain, so nothing here is tracked but
# the README.
/data/*
!/data/README.md

# Pipeline output. Each run writes its tables and provenance under data/sims/<system>/<run>,
# which the data/ rule above already ignores. The comparison figures results/README.md shows
# are tracked with their sidecars; the two diagnostic panels a run draws are not.
/results/*
!/results/README.md
!/results/*.png
!/results/*.pdf
!/results/*.toml
/results/residual_quantities.*
/results/charge_distribution.*

# Libraries do not pin a manifest; each environment resolves against [compat].
Manifest*.toml

# Julia artifacts
/docs/build/
*.cov
*.jl.mem
LocalPreferences.toml

# Editor and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*~
.DS_Store
